  m_Name: S07_Hazard_Blocked_Exit
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Valari.Data.TutorialData
  <Title>k__BackingField: "Identify Hazard 2 \u2014 Blocked Fire Exit"
  <Description>k__BackingField: Near the south wall you will see a fire exit door.
    A pallet has been left directly in front of it. A blocked fire exit is one of
    the most serious safety violations in any workplace. In an emergency, seconds
    matter, and a blocked exit can turn an evacuable situation into a fatal one.
    Fire exits must be kept clear at all times, even temporarily. There is no such
    thing as a short-term block. If you see a blocked exit, do not move the obstruction
    yourself if it involves heavy goods, report it immediately so it can be cleared
    safely. Log this hazard now.
  <VoiceOver>k__BackingField: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 0e25deda6335f20498a55b05b0ef30d5, type: 3}
  <HasChallenges>k__BackingField: 1
  <IsInOrder>k__BackingField: 1
  TutorialChallengeLists:
  - <ChallengeTitle>k__BackingField: Log the Blocked Fire Exit
    <ChallengeTriggerName>k__BackingField: TRIGGER_Safety_LogBlockedExit
    <IsComplete>k__BackingField: 0
